A||||3||LT1 Chop Top||88 gt 5-speed won't go into reverse||||1||
Z||000000||LT1 Chop Top||04-06-2001||08:02 PM||||All,<P>I am not able to get my 88 GT 5-speed into reverse, had trouble with that a bit last week, but then it just slid in and felt fine since...thought it was pilot error.  Any suggestions?  It also seems life 5th is having a difficult time engaging as well too.<P>Thanks for any suggestions.||||reg||1
Z||000001||85Josh||04-06-2001||08:50 PM||||Sounds like the select cable. Try adjusting it first, and hope it isn't broken. It could also be something jammed inside the shift mechanism in the tranny itself, this happened to me when I lost my speedo gear into the oil.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000002||PJ||04-06-2001||09:31 PM||||Reach in and see if you can shift it by moving the lever and push/pulling the shift shaft on the tranny case. When the select cable breaks you'll still be able to get 1 and 2 because those gears push the cable. 5th and reverse pull on the cable and won't work at all if the cable is broken.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by PJ (edited 04-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||04-06-2001||09:37 PM||||When my 88 was run out of oil in the tranny, it did the same thing. After a cool down and refill, it kind of shifted again. ||||reg||1
